 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? A good rule is to find spot in the shade near a water source. Many sites say in full sun, but a tent can heat up badly there. That's perfect. A tree will shade you from the midday sun, and you still get the afternoon breeze. That's dead or dying wood all over the place. It looks scary, but it won't hurt you. Avoid those. A fire can spread quickly and you' want get out fast. That's the basic rule. Add little more to the wind if it' usually gusty, and away from the edge in case the ground gives under your tent.",
